#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ead20b-1638-5e20-b8ae-c63ed579dd32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275793} {:answer/id #uuid "4a0d23eb-f670-5df0-be8c-a2e3beac9197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275794} {:answer/id #uuid "0fca5931-9374-5543-a9ff-2701cee97ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275795} {:answer/id #uuid "aa9e47d5-bfd0-5712-93b2-413a7c93a998" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275796} {:answer/id #uuid "40aebf18-4cef-50e6-8ed1-e0d0dbb1242b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fca5931-9374-5543-a9ff-2701cee97ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275795} :answer-field/id #uuid "be9f873f-41b2-5d03-bf29-080478d28cb0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fd36fc1-63ec-5bb6-9f2e-ae3a7bacac73" :question/math-academy-id "q-159757" :question/problem "If $z=-9-\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-9-\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=-9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(-9) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-9-\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-9+\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(-9-\\text{i})+(-9+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-9+(-9))+\\text{i}(-1+1) \\\\  & =-18+\\text{i}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275798 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "791c85f6-036e-5302-b391-62dada87e528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "97\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275800} {:answer/id #uuid "03a6240a-d4f7-531b-845f-02448db67f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275801} {:answer/id #uuid "4684b083-df53-50af-ba80-13a6e06b94f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275802} {:answer/id #uuid "b2579262-e10b-5a90-b3ee-f53be20c0c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275803} {:answer/id #uuid "df9e7888-d2be-5bd0-8330-508007d20767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "85\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275804}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2579262-e10b-5a90-b3ee-f53be20c0c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "97" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275803} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a75804f-d387-5b0f-abe7-fbe0278a0d9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275799}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36be1609-5bc0-56c1-a611-ac1989b2ace1" :question/math-academy-id "q-16423" :question/problem "Given that $z=4+9\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=4,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=9,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+{9}^{2} \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=4+9\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=4-9\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(4+9\\text{i})(4-9\\text{i}) \\\\  & ={4}^{2}+(4)(-9)\\text{i}+(4)(9)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(9)^{2} \\\\  & =16-36\\text{i}+36\\text{i}-(-1)(81) \\\\  & =16+81 \\\\  & =97.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275805 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1413da37-d531-576a-9d27-31157308f6eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1413da37-d531-576a-9d27-31157308f6eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275807} :answer-field/id #uuid "b307d44c-8fdb-53b6-81af-2885341cf98b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "594c5e35-b6c4-57d7-b7e2-3344f7754685" :question/math-academy-id "q-279477" :question/problem "If $z=-2-11\\text{i}$, then $z\\overset{―}{z}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-2-11\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-2,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-11,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-2)^{2}+(-11)^{2} \\\\  & =4+121 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-2-11\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-2+11\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-2-11\\text{i})(-2+11\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(2)^{2}+(-2)(11)\\text{i}+(-11)(-2)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(11)^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\cancel{22\\text{i}}+\\cancel{22\\text{i}}-(-1)(121) \\\\  & =25+100 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "64cd3ef1-6d41-50c6-b09d-cb709d89281f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Product of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "baad8b25-04ab-5022-a77d-328922d01009" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275810} {:answer/id #uuid "53607d26-c3cd-5553-b0da-e5e29b7ed499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275811} {:answer/id #uuid "acb1a52a-e383-5afb-9cf1-e7d33ce8a6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275812} {:answer/id #uuid "d9bad5ea-f670-527c-9f7e-ae4fc60956ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275813} {:answer/id #uuid "14416991-c1b6-56c4-8f07-f642ea4d2ab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "acb1a52a-e383-5afb-9cf1-e7d33ce8a6df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275812} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e302609-03d4-58f4-8887-8594b4dba452" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "786b081b-3937-58d9-97f1-dc3dd953af4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-72284" :question/problem "Given that $z=-1-7\\text{i}$, calculate $z\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we multiply a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always the sum of squares of the real part and the imaginary part.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ the real part is $\\text{Re}(z)=-1,$ and the imaginary part is $\\text{Im}(z)=-7,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(\\text{Re}(z))^{2}+(\\text{Im}(z))^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-7)^{2} \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of multiplying the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=-1-7\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=-1+7\\text{i}.$\n\nMultiplying, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z\\overset{―}{z} & =(-1-7\\text{i})(-1+7\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}+(-1)(7)\\text{i}+(-7)(-1)\\text{i}-{\\text{i}}^{2}(7)^{2} \\\\  & =1-7\\text{i}+7\\text{i}-(-1)(49) \\\\  & =1+49 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37a4168b-1425-5f3a-a577-4b5884906a52" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Complex Number and Its Conjugate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a820a3f-3505-55d1-8534-7cd8aef057c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275817} {:answer/id #uuid "20b87d01-5850-54fb-a0c0-3f41691aa9cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275818} {:answer/id #uuid "8f371e79-9272-5875-a7a5-dd41780164c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275819} {:answer/id #uuid "7115dfcd-b19a-5b49-9f09-a18780f7520d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275820} {:answer/id #uuid "dd234027-c6e2-5f25-bbe8-ac95697bea7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7115dfcd-b19a-5b49-9f09-a18780f7520d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275820} :answer-field/id #uuid "75b058af-2aa6-54b2-a5a4-88f1a395675b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b9d1a4c-4a3b-51d1-a470-99eb0d16e48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-8231" :question/problem "If $z=3-4\\text{i}$, calculate $z+\\overset{―}{z}.$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nWhen we add a complex number and its conjugate, the result is always twice the real part of the complex number.\n\nFor the given complex number $z=3-4\\text{i},$ the real part is $Re(z)=3,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =2\\text{Re}(z) \\\\  & =2(3) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nAlternatively, we can actually carry out the process of adding the complex number and its conjugate.\n\nTo obtain the conjugate of the complex number $z=3-4\\text{i},$ we flip the sign of the imaginary part and get $\\overset{―}{z}=3+4\\text{i}.$\n\nAdding, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+\\overset{―}{z} & =(3-4\\text{i})+(3+4\\text{i}) \\\\  & =(3+3)+\\text{i}(-4+4) \\\\  & =6+\\text{i}0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
